ound:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2023_a5gxuVH8Y0a9uyImGkqFOQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:CurrentPrepaymentsAndOtherCurrentAssets" scale="3" id="Tc_hyOXkJig50iSoh6jEplDKg_12_2">436,377</ix:nonFraction></b></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.41%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.5%;background:#cceeff;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_8Hl4eTAz2UibicoE-XXWqg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:CurrentPrepaymentsAndOtherCurrentAssets" scale="3" id="Tc__Q5onM0wEkGYWqSTrdriZg_12_4">204,177</ix:nonFraction></b></p></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:76.14%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">Included in assets classified as held for sale</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.41%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.51%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"> &#8212;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.41%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;">&#160;</p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.5%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_ifrs-full_ContinuingAndDiscontinuedOperationsAxis_ifrs-full_DisposalGroupsClassifiedAsHeldForSaleMember_CssegChy7ESJIGyQIxdi6w" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:CurrentPrepaymentsAndOtherCurrentAssets" scale="3" id="Tc_FCqp05NhdUiLXTGytJ5G7Q_13_4">19,342</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The credit quality of the financial assets included in prepayments, other receivables and other assets is considered to be &#8220;normal&#8221; when they are not past due and there is no information indicating that the financial assets had a significant increase in credit risk since initial recognition. Otherwise, the credit quality of the financial assets is considered to be &#8220;doubtful&#8221;.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">ECLs for the financial assets included in prepayments, other receivables and other assets are estimated by applying a loss rate approach with reference to the&#160;days past due for groupings of debtors with similar loss patterns. The loss rate is adjusted to reflect current conditions and forecasts of future economic conditions as appropriate.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of December 31, 2023 and 2024, for financial assets included in prepayments, other receivables and other assets with no significant increase in credit risk since initial recognition (Stage 1 of credit risk), the 12-month ECLs were estimated to be immaterial. Loss allowance was fully made for prepayments, other receivables and other assets with a significant increase in credit risk since initial recognition (Stage 3 of credit risk) or considered to be in default, amounting to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2023_ifrs-full_TypeOfMeasurementOfExpectedCreditLossesAxis_ifrs-full_TwelvemonthExpectedCreditLossesMember_naas_IfrsBalanceSheetLocationAxis_naas_PrepaymentsOtherReceivablesAndOtherAssetsMember_QA7rfMd8pEmbxJllUmYWXg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:MaximumExposureToCreditRiskOfFinancialAssets" scale="6" id="Narr_bEL1pkL1X0quveozQlG1ng">16.5</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_ifrs-full_TypeOfMeasurementOfExpectedCreditLossesAxis_ifrs-full_TwelvemonthExpectedCreditLossesMember_naas_IfrsBalanceSheetLocationAxis_naas_PrepaymentsOtherReceivablesAndOtherAssetsMember_rrlGhiTuoUmrB_feew8AMg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="ifrs-full:MaximumExposureToCreditRiskOfFinancialAssets" scale="6" id="Narr_vDlPBaop5UaFd1SxxE70uA">108.6</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million as of December 31, 2023 and 2024, respectively.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-42</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 15pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">NAAS TECHNOLOGY INC</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES&#160;TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-left:-10.0pt;margin-right:-10.0pt;max-width:100%;position:relative;width:calc(100% + 20.0pt);"><div style="padding-left:10pt;padding-right:10pt;position:relative;width:100%;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_Xl8RKcFSxEG8VnSZjirklg_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;">During the years ended December 31 2022, 2023 and 2024, loss allowance for prepayments, other receivables and other assets recognized in profit or loss amounted to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_r0WZAwVVWUiAws7Vp25qcA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="naas:LossAllowanceForPrepaymentsOtherReceivablesAndOtherAssets" scale="6" id="Narr_my3yeeLgDE-yXhc1gDhMHg">1.2</ix:nonFraction> million, RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_h-5RiJIdRUWk_UP9KnsQKQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="naas:LossAllowanceForPrepaymentsOtherReceivablesAndOtherAssets" scale="6" id="Narr_oALsTD1S_U61h1LINTzk9Q">20.1</ix:nonFraction> million and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_0qCbWPYWEEK2xacD2l1cCw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_gTXMK1-s4EOsKWmn_xm7UA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="naas:LossAllowanceForPrepaymentsOtherReceivablesAndOtherAssets" scale="6" id="Narr_s3LwTSHM1kCeCXBVi937Jg">73.1</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million, respectively.</p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><a id="_8560bddb_fd3a_4ed0_9dbc_a8e719cd8296"></a><a id="Tc_PX4hScHG0UyOb4DhV-bDAA_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_F5plVW3sxUicd_SGG4hYPw_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_kNL5yUGXm0KBxzoLkrCmhA_2_4"></a><a id="Tc__qrmH73hGEW8LG_M9Fs1Ug_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_cTVKQXCKAEWCtONhVvoZEQ_3_4"></a><a id="Tc_DCf9bYeFPUmELIaSeaK43w_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_vofKIDRW7k6N0jAk_lYRxw_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_f7T_7Bgpb0y50uwUMXL7eQ_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_rDowQsPubEqeF3uMe-htDA_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_9ZniCUXZp0uZDBXoUYmNDA_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_teAAkfuqUU6-hfa9i_BxKw_10_0"></a><a id="Tc_XFZV_ac9KE-FgvXe5MtqmQ_11_0"></a><a id="Tc_z32MR_-waE-jZ5EK3NAALQ_12_0"></a><a id="Tc_uJjajjRqdkGgfwDOLfwnQA_13_0"></a><a id="_4f840fff_2a55_47c5_aa18_69ec764205ff"></a><a id="Tc_T9Fs4fiRnEOGBByjEpijEg_1_0"></a><a id="Tc_k1augRo_n0WG7ErGNZ4lXA_2_0"></a><a id="Tc_arqVFyL2Q0y5EXjdvBfYbw_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_BaGB3G7lqU2wsBDR55Efiw_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_xOwSuUO6hk2VvBrEOq5kmw_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_lTSZkhBoPEaUwzjnPeBD7g_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_fhmLHhO4QE-aowB29y5oBw_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_eJ4qRyW2YEqBeonQj8dGEQ_8_0"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_gTXMK1-s4EOsKWmn_xm7UA" name="ifrs-full:DisclosureOfFinancialInstrumentsExplanatory" id="Tb_6LcsVAATT0as626ZFTFEmw" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="display:inline-block;text-indent:0pt;width:18pt;"><b style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight: